, underwater image enhancement (UIE), and image signal processing (ISP).\n\n### Model Efficiency\n\nThe model achieves remarkable compactness with only ~4K parameters (0.02 MB) and 0.924 GFLOPs computational cost. Inference speeds reach 1,120 FPS on GPU and up to 1,100 FPS on mobile SoC (Snapdragon 8 Gen 3), corresponding to inference latency of ~0.9-14.4 ms depending on the task.\n\n### Enhancement Quality\n\nDespite extreme lightweight design, MobileIE delivers competitive or superior image quality metrics:\n\n  * Low-light enhancement: 23.62 PSNR, 0.812 SSIM on LOLv1; 25.08 PSNR, 0.845 SSIM on LOLv2-Real\n  * Underwater enhancement: 22.81 PSNR, 0.906 SSIM on UIEB dataset\n  * ISP: 21.43 PSNR, 0.731 SSIM on ZRR dataset\n\nThe model consistently achieves the highest \"SCORE\" (comprehensive performance-efficiency metric) across all tasks, outperforming significantly larger and slower alternatives.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMobileIE: An Extremely Lightweight and Effective ConvNet for Real-Time Image Enhancement on Mobile Devices (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/404405122_MobileIE_An_Extremely_Lightweight_and_Effective_ConvNet_for_Real-Time_Image_Enhancement_on_Mobile_Devices?_tp=eyJjb250ZXh0Ijp7InBhZ2UiOiJzY2llbnRpZmljQ29udHJpYnV0aW9ucyIsInByZXZpb3VzUGFnZSI6bnVsbCwic3ViUGFnZSI6bnVsbH19)\nciteturn37search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; # MobileIE: An Extremely Lightweight and Effective ConvNet for Real-Time Image Enhancement on Mobile Devices\n\n# MobileIE: An Extremely Lightweight and Effective ConvNet for Real-Time Image Enhancement on Mobile Devices\n\n  * October 2025\n\nDOI:10.1109/ICCV51701.2025.02038\n\n  * Conference: 2025 IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)\n\nAuthors:\n\nHailong Yan\n\n  * University of Electronic Science and Technology of China\n\nAo Li\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research